# Integration

Add the library to any CMake project (host, STM32, RP2040, nRF, ...), and choose its defaults with Kconfig.

## CMake (any MCU, any host)

```cmake
add_subdirectory(external/@REPO@)
target_link_libraries(my_app PRIVATE xmpl100::xmpl100)
```

Or install it and use the package; the target name is the same:

```bash
cmake -S external/@REPO@ -B build-lib && cmake --install build-lib --prefix /opt/sdk
```

```cmake
find_package(xmpl100 0.1 REQUIRED)            # with CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=/opt/sdk
target_link_libraries(my_app PRIVATE xmpl100::xmpl100)
```

Headers are included through the one include root: `#include "@ROOT@/MovingAverage.h"`.

| Option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `XMPL100_ENABLE_WARNINGS` | `OFF` | `-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic` on every target that links the library |
| `XMPL100_BUILD_TESTS` | `OFF` | Builds the host tests ([Testing and CI](testing.md)) |

