## ESP-IDF

Under ESP-IDF the root [`CMakeLists.txt`](../CMakeLists.txt) registers the repository itself as a component
(`ESP_PLATFORM`: `idf_component_register()` with [`_config/Kconfig`](../_config/Kconfig)). Add the checkout to
`EXTRA_COMPONENT_DIRS`, put it under `components/`, or use it as a component-manager git dependency:

```yaml
# main/idf_component.yml of your project
dependencies:
  xmpl100:
    git: https://github.com/@ORG@/@REPO@.git
    version: v0.1.0
```

ESP-IDF names a component after its folder (or, through the component manager, after the key), so your component
declares `REQUIRES xmpl100` or the folder name. There is no `idf_component.yml` in the repository: it is only
needed to publish to the ESP Component Registry, and is added at the root if that is chosen.
<!-- /scaffold:platform-esp32 -->

## Kconfig

Under ESP-IDF, menuconfig shows **@TITLE@** ([`_config/Kconfig`](../_config/Kconfig)). The values reach the code
only through
[`inc/@ROOT@/Kconfig.h`](../inc/@ROOT@/Kconfig.h):

```cpp
--8<-- "tests/docs/api_tasks.cpp:kconfig"
```

| Option | Default | `Config` field |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `CONFIG_XMPL100_WINDOW_SAMPLES` | 8 | `window_samples` |

## Version

The version is set once in [`cmake/xmpl100_build_settings.cmake`](../cmake/xmpl100_build_settings.cmake)
and generated into `@ROOT@/Version.h`; `xmpl100::GetVersion()` returns it.
